    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm having a massive headache with our jenkins pipeline. we've got these incredibly flaky unit tests in the staging environment. the code hasn't changed, but the build stage fails intermittently with weird, non-deterministic errors in the logs. sometimes it's a timeout, sometimes it's a weird connection reset. any idea how i can start isolating if this is an environmental issue or something else?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Flaky tests in staging, especially with intermittent timeouts and connection resets, often point to environment instability. You should start by checking your staging environment's resource utilization—CPU, memory, and network latency—during the build runs. If the resources are fluctuating wildly, it's likely the infrastructure itself is the culprit, not the code. A good first step is to run the tests locally against a local, isolated instance of your staging environment to see if the flakiness persists.",
