    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i'll look into the pod events, thanks. it's just so frustrating because there's no pattern at all. it's like something is actively sabotaging the build every now and then. do you think it's possible for a race condition in the network layer to cause something this erratic? or is it more likely a hardware fluke?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A race condition in the network layer is absolutely possible, especially if your tests are hammering a shared service or if the underlying networking fabric is under stress. It's less likely to be a pure hardware fluke, though old, poorly maintained hardware can certainly behave like one. I'd suggest adding more detailed, high-frequency logging around the network calls within your unit tests themselves. If you can pinpoint *exactly* when the connection resets happen relative to the test execution flow, you might catch the timing window.",
      "source": "target",
